			(property "MPN" "TSOP38438"
				(at 0 0 0)
				(hide yes)
				(effects
					(font
						(size 1.27 1.27)
					)
				)
			)
			(property "Package" "Minicast leaded, 5.0 W x 6.95 H x 4.8 D mm, 1 = OUT, 2 = GND, 3 = VS"
				(at 0 0 0)
				(hide yes)
				(effects
					(font
						(size 1.27 1.27)
					)
				)
			)
			(property "Note" "Verified against Vishay document 82491 Rev 2.1, 27-May-2025 (TSOP382.., TSOP384..) in FBV2-S1-007. Same Minicast package, same pinning 1 = OUT, 2 = GND, 3 = VS and the same footprint as the TSOP38238 it replaces, so this is a pure MPN change. VS 2.0 to 5.5 V, ISD 0.25 / 0.35 / 0.45 mA at 3.3 V, output ACTIVE LOW with a 30 kOhm INTERNAL pull-up shown in the block diagram, so no external pull-up is required and OUT drives a GPIO directly. VOSL 30 mV typ at 0.5 mA. Directivity plus/minus 45 degrees. Absolute maximum VS 6 V, IO 5 mA. Carrier 38 kHz with a 3 dB bandwidth of f0/10, i.e. f0 plus/minus 5 percent, so 36.1 to 39.9 kHz; relative responsivity is about 0.75 at 36 kHz (RC5/RC6) and about 0.72 at 40 kHz (Sony), which costs roughly 13 to 15 percent of range on those carriers. THE 4 IN TSOP38438 IS THE AGC VARIANT, NOT A PACKAGE CODE. AGC4 is the higher AGC setting: Vishay states that the higher the AGC the better noise is suppressed but the lower the code compatibility. In the suitable-data-format table AGC4 is marked Preferred for NEC, RC5/RC6, Thomson RCA, Sharp and Mitsubishi and adds Fig. 15 high-modulation fluorescent suppression that AGC2 does not have - but it is marked NO for Sony code, where the AGC2 TSOP38238 is marked Yes. This affects RECEIVE ONLY. Transmitting Sony SIRC is unaffected because the transmitter is just a carrier and timing from the MCU. The TSOP38238 symbol is retained in this library so switching back to AGC2 is a lib_id change and nothing else."
				(at 0 0 0)
				(hide yes)
				(effects
					(font
						(size 1.27 1.27)
					)
				)
			)
