	(text "IR TRANSMITTER - MIGRATED FBV2-S1-007\n\nD1 = VISHAY TSAL6100  940 nm, +/-10 deg, Ie 170 mW/sr\n  FALLBACK TSAL6200 IS A DROP-IN: SAME PACKAGE,\n  SAME VF, SAME IFM, SAME R24. Ie 72 mW/sr, +/-17 deg.\n\nPEAK CURRENT = 150 mA.\n  THE LIMIT IS IFM = 200 mA, THE REPETITIVE RATING\n  AT tp/T = 0.5. IFSM = 1.5 A IS A SINGLE PULSE OF\n  <= 5 us AND MUST NOT BE USED FOR 38 kHz CARRIER.\n  100 mA  50% of IFM   170 mW/sr\n  150 mA  75% of IFM   ~255 mW/sr   <-- SELECTED\n  200 mA  100% of IFM  no tolerance margin left\n  300 mA  150% of IFM  OUT OF SPEC, REJECTED\n\nSUPPLY = +3V3, NOT SYS.\n  REGULATED +/-2% GIVES 118-170 mA ACROSS ALL\n  TOLERANCES. ON SYS 3.2-5.0 V THE SAME RESISTOR\n  GIVES 64-166 mA, A 2.6:1 SWING, AND IR RANGE\n  WOULD VISIBLY SHORTEN AS THE BATTERY DRAINS.\n  THE 38 kHz DISTURBANCE IS BOUNDED BY C12 AND THE\n  ONLY 38 kHz-SENSITIVE PART, U6, SITS BEHIND 41 dB.\n\nR24 = 12R 1% 0805   I = (3.3 - 1.50 - 0.005) / 12\nR123 = DNP PARALLEL TRIM. NEVER BELOW 10R TOTAL.\nC12 = 22 uF 1210, >= 15 uF EFFECTIVE AT 3.3 V BIAS\n  -> ~40 mV OF 38 kHz ON THE RAIL.\n\nQ1 AO3400A CONFIRMED 1=G 2=S 3=D FROM THE AOS\nDATASHEET. R23 100k HOLDS THE GATE AT <= 10 mV\nAGAINST A 650 mV THRESHOLD: NO IR AT BOOT OR RESET."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 340 60 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "bc571da3-1e81-440e-93a9-596905c531bf")
	)
	(text "IR RECEIVER - MIGRATED FBV2-S1-007\nRECEIVER CORRECTED FBV2-S1-008\n\nU6 = VISHAY TSOP38238  38 kHz, AGC2\n  VS 2.0-5.5 V, 0.35 mA TYP, OUTPUT ACTIVE LOW,\n  30k INTERNAL PULL-UP SO NO EXTERNAL ONE IS NEEDED.\n  ACCEPTANCE +/-45 deg.\n  TSOP38438 (AGC4) IS A DOCUMENTED DROP-IN FALLBACK:\n  SAME MINICAST BODY, SAME 1=OUT/2=GND/3=VS PINNING,\n  SAME FOOTPRINT, SAME ELECTRICAL TABLE.\n\nSUPPLY FILTER R21 100R + C11 4.7uF IS CORRECT AND\nIS THE REASON THE TX CAN SHARE +3V3:\n  fc = 339 Hz  ->  41 dB AT 38 kHz\n  DATASHEET FIG 7: THE RECEIVER DEGRADES FROM ABOUT\n  10 mV RMS OF SUPPLY RIPPLE AT THE CARRIER, AND\n  DOUBLES ITS THRESHOLD BY 50 mV. 40 mV ON THE RAIL\n  BECOMES 0.1 mV HERE. ~90x MARGIN.\n\nBANDWIDTH: 3 dB AT f0/10, SO 36.1-39.9 kHz.\n  38 kHz NEC/SAMSUNG/SHARP/MITSUBISHI  1.00\n  36 kHz RC5/RC6                       ~0.75\n  40 kHz SONY                          ~0.72\n\nO-5 IS CLOSED. THE CTO RULED FOR AGC2.\nAGC2 IS MARKED YES FOR ALL SIX LISTED PROTOCOLS\nINCLUDING SONY; AGC4 IS MARKED **NO** FOR SONY.\nMECHANISM: AFTER A BURST > 10 CYCLES AGC2 NEEDS A\nGAP > 5x THE BURST AND TAKES 10-70 CYCLES/BURST,\nAGC4 NEEDS > 15x AND TAKES ONLY 10-35. SIRC BREAKS\nTHE AGC4 LIMIT.\nCOST OF THE REVERT: AGC4 FIG 15 HIGH-MODULATION\nFLUORESCENT SUPPRESSION IS LOST. AGC2 HAS FIG 14.\n\nPLACEMENT (MECHANICAL, NOT ELECTRICAL):\nKEEP U6 PHYSICALLY SEPARATED FROM D1, OUTSIDE THE\nLED EMISSION CONE, BEHIND AN OPAQUE BARRIER,\n>= 15 mm APART. KEEP THE TX CURRENT LOOP AWAY FROM\nTHE RECEIVER SUPPLY AND RETURN."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 340 165 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "cf320489-f52c-4fc9-9633-6900b1d56c23")
	)
