		(property "Package" "Minicast leaded, 5.0 W x 6.95 H x 4.8 D mm, 1 = OUT, 2 = GND, 3 = VS"
			(at 99.06 72.39 0)
			(hide yes)
			(show_name no)
			(do_not_autoplace no)
			(effects
				(font
					(size 1.27 1.27)
				)
			)
		)
		(property "Note" "RECEIVER REVERTED TSOP38438 -> TSOP38238 in FBV2-S1-008 by CTO ruling on the O-5 item raised at FBV2-S1-007. TSOP38238 is the AGC2 part and is the FITTED first build; TSOP38438 (AGC4) is retained as a DOCUMENTED DROP-IN FALLBACK and its symbol stays in the project library. Verified against Vishay document 82491 Rev 2.1, 27-May-2025: both MPNs appear in the SAME parts table sharing the Minicast package, the pinning 1 = OUT / 2 = GND / 3 = VS, the body 5.0 W x 6.95 H x 4.8 D mm, leaded mounting and one shared electrical table - so this is a pure MPN change and the footprint, the R21/C11 supply filter and every FBV2-S1-007 calculation are unaffected. VS 2.0 to 5.5 V; ISD 0.25 / 0.35 / 0.45 mA at VS = 3.3 V; output ACTIVE LOW with a 30 kOhm INTERNAL pull-up so OUT drives GPIO44 directly and no external pull-up is needed; directivity plus/minus 45 deg; f0 = 38 kHz with a 3 dB bandwidth of f0/10, i.e. 36.1 to 39.9 kHz. WHY AGC2 IS THE RIGHT FIRST BUILD: the suitable-data-format table marks AGC2 Yes for NEC, RC5/RC6, Thomson RCA 56 kHz, Sharp, SONY and Mitsubishi, where AGC4 is marked NO for Sony code. The mechanism is the gap requirement - after a burst longer than 10 cycles AGC2 needs a gap of more than 5 x the burst length and accepts 10 to 70 cycles per burst, while AGC4 needs more than 15 x and accepts only 10 to 35 - and Sony SIRC violates the AGC4 limit. WHAT IS GIVEN UP: AGC4 adds the Fig. 15 suppression of high-modulation fluorescent-lamp interference that AGC2 (Fig. 14 only) does not have. That is the whole cost of the revert, and it is a fluorescent-lighting robustness margin rather than a protocol."
			(at 99.06 72.39 0)
			(hide yes)
			(show_name no)
			(do_not_autoplace no)
			(effects
				(font
					(size 1.27 1.27)
				)
			)
		)
