		(property "Package" "T-1 3/4 leaded, 5 mm diameter, 2.54 mm lead pitch"
			(at 196.85 73.66 0)
			(hide yes)
			(show_name no)
			(do_not_autoplace no)
			(effects
				(font
					(size 1.27 1.27)
				)
			)
		)
		(property "Note" "IR EMITTER LOCKED TSAL6100 in FBV2-S1-007, replacing the inherited TSAL6200. Verified against Vishay document 81009 Rev 1.8. 940 nm GaAlAs MQW, T-1 3/4 leaded, 5 mm diameter. Ie 170 mW/sr typ (80 min) at IF = 100 mA, ANGLE OF HALF INTENSITY plus/minus 10 degrees, radiant power 40 mW, tr/tf 15 ns. VF 1.35 V typ / 1.6 V max at 100 mA. THE BINDING LIMIT FOR 38 kHz REMOTE USE IS IFM = 200 mA, the REPETITIVE peak rating at tp/T = 0.5 with tp = 100 us. IFSM = 1.5 A is a SINGLE-PULSE surge for t <= 5 us and MUST NOT be used to justify repetitive carrier current. Continuous IF is 100 mA, PV 160 mW, RthJA 230 K/W, Tj 100 C. Selected first-build peak is 150 mA, 75 percent of IFM; worst case across rail, VF and resistor tolerance is 170 mA, still 15 percent below IFM. Average LED power over an NEC frame is about 25 mW against a 160 mW limit, so Tj rises about 6 K. TSAL6200 IS A DROP-IN FALLBACK: identical T-1 3/4 package and footprint, identical VF 1.35/1.6 at 100 mA and identical IFM 200 mA, so R24 needs no change. It trades Ie 170 -> 72 mW/sr for a beam of plus/minus 17 instead of plus/minus 10 degrees. Fit it if first-article testing shows the TSAL6100 cone is too narrow to aim comfortably."
			(at 196.85 73.66 0)
			(hide yes)
			(show_name no)
			(do_not_autoplace no)
			(effects
				(font
					(size 1.27 1.27)
				)
			)
		)
